AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::removeRewardToken()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount before external reward checks
├── when token is not configured
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput without calling reward pool or token
├── when token is the reward pool primary reward token
│   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput without querying token balance
├── when token has a nonzero market balance
│   ├── when balance is one smallest token unit
│   │   └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
│   └── when balance is larger
│       └── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput
├── when reward pool rewardToken query reverts or returns malformed data
│   └── it should propagate the failure without changing the list
├── when token balanceOf reverts or returns malformed data
│   └── it should propagate the failure without changing the list
├── given a configured non-primary token with zero balance
│   ├── when token is the last list element
│   │   └── it should pop the last element without changing earlier order
│   ├── when token is the first or middle list element
│   │   └── it should move the prior last token into the removed index and pop the list
│   ├── it should decrease the reward-token array length
│   ├── it should set isRewardToken for the removed token to false
│   ├── it should preserve membership for every remaining token
│   ├── it should emit RewardTokenRemoved
│   ├── it should not transfer or claim any token
│   ├── it should allow the removed token to be added again later
│   ├── it should exclude the removed token from later claims even if Convex distributes it again
│   └── it should not change market accounting or Convex custody
├── when reward pool reports a different primary token after initialization
│   ├── it should protect the currently reported primary token from removal
│   └── it should treat the formerly reported primary token as removable if its balance is zero
└── when market is paused frozen or Convex inactive
    └── it should remain callable by owner subject to the same token checks
